- written informed consent;

- consent to use of effective contraception methods during the whole period of
participation in the study; (using one of the following methods: abstinence, condoms
(male or female with or without spermicide), diaphragm or cervical cap with a
spermicidal tool, intrauterine device);

- body mass index (BMI) is 18.5 ≤ BMI ≤ 30;

- absence of acute infections/exacerbations of chronic at the time of participation in
the study and for 7 days before initiation of therapy;

- absence of allergic disease severe disease (anaphylaxis, angioedema, polymorphic
exudative eczema, serum sickness);

- no history of severe complications in a previous application of immunobiological
