- the use of other drugs based on murine monoclonal antibodies in history;

- regular past or current use of narcotic drugs;

- pregnancy or breast-feeding;

- systolic blood pressure less than 100 mm of mercury.St. or above 139 mm Hg.St;
diastolic blood pressure less than 60 mm of mercury.St. or higher 90 mm. Hg.St.; heart
