Trial: NCT00825435
Title: Coronary CT Angiography in Acute Chest Pain is a Cost Effective Risk Stratification Strategy
Conditions: Acute Chest Pain
Interventions: Coronary CT Angiogram
Phase: Phase 3
Summary: This study will evaluate the impact of adding coronary computed tomographic angiography (CTA)
on health care costs for diagnosing patients with acute chest pain.
Eligibility: sex All; age 35 Years to N/A; healthy volunteers Accepts Healthy Volunteers
Criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:

- patients who complain of typical or atypical chest pain (that is compatible with
ischemia during the past 12 hrs);

